WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.500
Cells break down food to build ATP, a molecule that carries energy to cell work.

2
00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.440
With oxygen, most ATP is made in the mitochondria.

3
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:14.760
This is cellular respiration.

4
00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:18.340
It matters because every working cell needs energy.

5
00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:20.220
A muscle cell pulls.

6
00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:22.940
A nerve cell pumps charged particles.

7
00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.100
Cells build proteins.

8
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.280
Glucose is a sugar.

9
00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:31.080
With oxygen, it becomes carbon dioxide and water.

10
00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:34.680
Much of the released energy is captured in ATP.

11
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:36.580
Some leaves as heat.

12
00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:39.180
The first steps happen in the cytoplasm.

13
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:44.920
Later steps happen in mitochondria, organelles in plant, animal and fungal cells.

14
00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:47.160
Plants respire too.

15
00:00:47.883 --> 00:00:50.383
ATP has three phosphate groups in a row.

16
00:00:51.243 --> 00:00:54.803
When ATP reacts with water, the end phosphate group comes off.

17
00:00:55.663 --> 00:00:58.363
What is left is ADP, with two phosphate groups.

18
00:00:59.203 --> 00:01:02.783
The whole reaction releases energy that the cell uses for work.

19
00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.063
Breaking a bond takes energy.

20
00:01:05.903 --> 00:01:07.223
ATP is not energy.

21
00:01:08.103 --> 00:01:10.083
It is a molecule that carries energy.

22
00:01:11.083 --> 00:01:14.283
Putting a phosphate group back onto ADP takes energy.

23
00:01:15.563 --> 00:01:17.723
Cellular respiration supplies that energy.

24
00:01:18.503 --> 00:01:20.963
So ATP and ADP go round in a cycle.

25
00:01:22.043 --> 00:01:23.743
Cell work turns ATP into ADP.

26
00:01:24.823 --> 00:01:27.323
Respiration turns ADP back into ATP.

27
00:01:28.203 --> 00:01:32.583
A cell keeps only a small supply of ATP, so it rebuilds it all the time.

28
00:01:33.567 --> 00:01:35.447
Aerobic means using oxygen.

29
00:01:36.407 --> 00:01:37.927
Anaerobic means without oxygen.

30
00:01:38.847 --> 00:01:41.827
Without oxygen, muscle cells and yeast use fermentation.

31
00:01:42.947 --> 00:01:45.607
The SOL calls this anaerobic respiration.

32
00:01:46.507 --> 00:01:51.287
With oxygen, an animal cell gets about thirty to thirty-two ATP per glucose.

33
00:01:52.387 --> 00:01:53.767
Fermentation gives only two.

34
00:01:54.627 --> 00:01:56.847
In muscle, fermentation makes lactate.

35
00:01:57.627 --> 00:02:00.247
In yeast, it makes ethanol and carbon dioxide.

36
00:02:00.247 --> 00:02:04.107
The carbon dioxide forms the bubbles that make dough rise.

37
00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:10.630
Photosynthesis uses light energy to build glucose from carbon dioxide and water.

38
00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:12.730
It releases oxygen.

39
00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:18.390
Respiration breaks glucose down with oxygen into carbon dioxide and water.

40
00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:22.510
Plants do both. The atoms go round and round.

41
00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:25.750
Energy arrives as light and leaves as heat.

42
00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:30.130
Along the way, ATP carries energy from food to cell work.
